      "MOLLY: If they say they’re interested in poker you give them my number. I vet them. If they end up playing in the game I’ll give you a thousand dol…\nCLUB GIRL: Is this true?",
      "MOLLY: I could stake her, infiltrate other games and poach their big ticket players. She could glance at a table and tell you how much money was on…\nJESSE: Six-hundred and forty-thousand, eight-hundred dollars.\nMOLLY: Not even close.\nJESSE: No, that’s how much is left in the bag.",
      "MOLLY: Shelby could write code and was a decent hacker. Right now I’ve asked her to tell me my account balance at B of A.\nMOLLY: You got it yet or are you playing Minecraft?\nSHELBY: Playing Minecraft.\nMOLLY: Shelby--",
      "MOLLY: Winston would be working for the CIA if she could pass a drug test. She was the daughter of an American diplomat who’s lived in nine differe…\nMOLLY: Who’s the biggest game in Manhattan and what are the stakes?\nWINSTON: On any given night it’s either Eddie Ting or Irv Gotti. 50K buy- in, blinds are one-thousand/two- thousand.\nMOLLY: Right.",
      "MOLLY: Which three poems?\nSTELLA: “Close”, “Rush” and “Walls”."
